{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00056 - MONDO_18434",
  "verbalization": "Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin is clinically indicated for Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) with Npm1 or Cebpa somatic mutations, and it is also associated with AML with T(9;11)(p22;q23) through a shared pathway involving Idarubicin. The evidence suggests that Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin may exert its therapeutic effect by influencing the same molecular pathways that are implicated in AML with T(9;11)(p22;q23), potentially through a mechanism that involves the interaction with the cell surface and subsequent intracellular signaling. The presence of a common downstream target, Idarubicin, further supports the notion that Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin may act in a manner that is relevant to the pathogenesis of AML with T(9;11)(p22;q23). The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin to be a candidate for repositioning in AML with this specific chromosomal abnormality, provided that the underlying mechanisms are sufficiently well-characterized and that the observed associations are not coincidental.",
